think The round-open named three files orphan:work in stash@{0} -- tools/fixtures/r/record_version_scan.sh, its control, and tools/r/record_version_witness.rish -- beside an unlanded session log and a shelved account. That is a whole lap of mine, stamped 20260917.050525, cut between its staging and its commit. My claim pheromone-record-version-census still read status=building on the live board, which is the same fact from the other side.
think So this lap is a recovery rather than a new build, and the one honest question is whether the parked bytes still hold. Every reading was RE-RUN on metal rather than carried across: record_version_scan.sh reads 32 counted families over 84 sites, one chronological, two domain, seven unclassified each printed by name; the pen runs 21 legs with 0 failing and four mutations bitten; tools/r/record_version_witness.rish is GREEN off the built rishi.
think The card needed room before the account could land. HEAD's construction/ITINERARY.md stood 29 bytes under its 40,960-byte ceiling and this lap's account put it 436 over. The three-line BAKERY THE THIRD PATH IN THE KEY pointer folds: its account already stands whole on construction/archive/20260916-093400_itinerary-landed-accounts.md and the card itself records its one ask as answered. Cairn written to construction/CHECKPOINTS.md at walk-back nib 9d0868ef6d before the cut, and my own account tightened by roughly 200 bytes rather than folding a peer's live question.
obs A stale roster pass held construction/standing-equipment-run.lock.d from the previous lap, launched at ba8dddfc9e, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved. The runner names the repair on its own face -- kill -TERM <pid> runs its EXIT trap and releases the lock -- and the pid came from the lock directory rather than from a command-line pattern, which is the difference the baton's eighth firing was about. Checked /proc/<pid>/cwd against this tree before signalling.
obs A build survives its own lap's death only because fleet_round_open.sh stashes rather than discards, and only because stash_record_scan.sh names what stands on no ref. Neither is a guard and both are readers; together they are the reason no work was lost.
obs Grades at Meter: scan B+/88, control B+/86, witness B+/86, the card A+/100 with its ordered-list shadow reported.
obs The cold endurance run read 22 red and the hot 18, the four between them closed by this lap: readme_metrics regenerated after staging, fold_shelf_link and fold_shelf_link_repoint by running the rostered repointer over grass's shelf, and remember_git_nib by carrying the nib into this work commit. Of the 18 that stand, none is mine -- ratchet_slack's one uncompared ceiling is awk_lcg_exact, standing_equipment cascades from instrument_refusal's recorded red, and record_version reads compared=yes in the same census.
rota lap 5280, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears: listen for the page nobody answered. foundations/20260826-024942_the-grain-and-the-crossing.md answers my own account's standing ask from canon rather than from taste: its fifth strand reads *accretion on one clock -- names endure, growth arrives beside what stands, versions are chronological, later is larger*. So the molt of 32 counted record families is a GRAIN question, cutting with a seated strand, rather than a style preference -- and the page's own strand count is derived by a witness for exactly the reason the census exists.
